WEBVTT

00:32.420 --> 00:34.630
Oh? Hello.

00:53.610 --> 00:55.110
You've still got a long way to go.

00:55.110 --> 00:57.990
If that's all you've got, then my little brother is better than you.

00:57.990 --> 00:59.800
Quit kidding around.

00:59.800 --> 01:01.620
Hiro is still in elementary school, isn't he?

01:01.620 --> 01:04.000
Do you think I'd lie?

01:05.330 --> 01:07.210
Fine, I got it...

01:07.210 --> 01:10.500
If it was a landscape, then I'd pull it off somehow, but...

01:10.500 --> 01:12.810
If you want to go into design,

01:12.810 --> 01:15.070
then you'd better be able to draw any genre.

01:15.070 --> 01:20.220
For a plaster figure, the distinction between a figure and a still-life is vague, so it's difficult.

01:20.220 --> 01:24.020
If you're tired of drawing plaster figures,
do you want to try a nude sketch instead?

01:24.020 --> 01:24.930
No!

01:24.930 --> 01:26.770
I want to draw plaster figures.

01:26.770 --> 01:29.020
So which is it? Seriously.

01:31.470 --> 01:32.820
Sorry, Nagi.

01:32.820 --> 01:33.980
About what?

01:33.980 --> 01:38.280
In reality, I'm not exactly in a position to ask you to do things like this.

01:38.280 --> 01:41.630
I don't like to be bound by disturbing feelings.

01:41.630 --> 01:45.500
Besides, it's enjoyable to teach you art like this.

01:46.390 --> 01:47.500
Sorry.

01:47.500 --> 01:50.980
If you really feel sorry, then hurry up and improve.

01:50.980 --> 01:52.750
Or else I'm going to make you do nude sketches.

02:01.040 --> 02:01.890
I'm home.

02:02.160 --> 02:04.110
Welcome home, Yu-kun!

02:04.110 --> 02:06.060
Your supper is ready.

02:08.560 --> 02:10.250
This is delicious.

02:10.250 --> 02:13.450
The landlord gave me these eggs.

02:13.450 --> 02:14.570
The landlord?

02:14.770 --> 02:18.360
Apparently, they're from the chickens he raises.

02:18.360 --> 02:19.530
I see.

02:19.530 --> 02:21.400
We ought to thank him.

02:21.400 --> 02:23.870
His twin grandchildren delivered them to us.

02:24.140 --> 02:26.000
Kei-chan and Chihiro-chan.

02:26.000 --> 02:28.790
They look so similar, and they're both so cute!

02:28.790 --> 02:31.420
I want kids like that!

02:31.420 --> 02:33.410
Now's the only time they'll be cute.

02:33.410 --> 02:37.420
Sooner or later, they grow up and start to talk back.

02:37.420 --> 02:40.430
Geez, you're completely tactless.

02:40.430 --> 02:43.170
I can survive without tact.

02:43.170 --> 02:47.680
In this age, if you lack sensitivity, you can't get a job.

02:48.430 --> 02:52.120
My senior at my part-time job said that.

02:52.120 --> 02:58.070
Well, the storekeeper asked <i>me, the insensitive guy, if I wanted to work for them after I graduate.</i>

02:58.070 --> 03:00.230
Oh? Really?

03:00.230 --> 03:03.070
Yeah, but I asked him if I could have some time to think about it.

03:03.070 --> 03:07.200
I see. Because you're aiming for the top, aren't you, Yu-kun?

03:08.690 --> 03:10.620
I gave up on that.

03:11.790 --> 03:16.500
I'm not aiming up anymore. Now, I'm aiming forward.

03:16.720 --> 03:17.740
Forward...

03:21.510 --> 03:24.410
Yuko, are you happy right now?

03:24.410 --> 03:26.300
Why are you asking that out of the blue?

03:26.300 --> 03:27.990
Please tell me.

03:27.990 --> 03:30.150
I'm happy.

03:30.150 --> 03:32.870
I've been freed from inescapable suffering,

03:32.870 --> 03:35.800
and I'm living with the person I've always admired.

03:35.800 --> 03:38.950
I'd be lying if I said that the past isn't painful,

03:38.950 --> 03:42.150
but you've even accepted those wounds.

03:42.410 --> 03:44.910
You saved everything about me.

03:47.870 --> 03:49.240
Yuko...

03:49.240 --> 03:51.370
Thank you, Yu-kun.

03:52.440 --> 03:55.710
I want to protect the present.

03:55.710 --> 03:56.840
The present?

03:56.840 --> 04:00.860
Yeah. I want to continue to protect you and the happiness you feel right now.

04:00.860 --> 04:02.280
That's why...

04:02.280 --> 04:03.960
It's not about looking up or down.

04:03.960 --> 04:05.640
It's not about winning or losing.

04:06.150 --> 04:09.260
I just want to walk forward with you.

04:10.470 --> 04:12.140
Yu-kun...

04:13.940 --> 04:15.560
Let's go together, okay?

04:15.560 --> 04:16.770
Yes!

04:24.830 --> 04:26.530
Is someone there?

04:30.290 --> 04:31.680
A child?

04:31.680 --> 04:33.910
What's wrong, so late at night?

04:36.880 --> 04:38.500
A girl from the orphanage?

04:40.500 --> 04:42.550
What's your name?

04:43.780 --> 04:46.940
My name is Yuko, Amamiya Yuko.

04:46.940 --> 04:48.640
What's yours?

04:50.100 --> 04:51.390
Miki.

04:51.390 --> 04:53.140
Miki?

04:53.140 --> 04:55.640
It's written like "Mirai", and read "Miki".

04:53.140 --> 04:55.640
"Mirai" means "future".

04:55.860 --> 04:57.030
I see.

04:57.030 --> 04:59.770
What's wrong, Miki-chan? Why are you out so late?

05:01.730 --> 05:03.930
I'll call one of the teachers from the orphanage.

05:03.930 --> 05:05.400
Yuko, please look after her.

05:05.400 --> 05:06.400
No!

05:07.660 --> 05:11.160
No! Please... keep them away from me!

05:16.010 --> 05:18.980
This happens to kids who are new to the orphanage.

05:18.980 --> 05:21.630
They're not used to the change in their surroundings yet.

05:21.630 --> 05:24.380
That doesn't seem to be the issue.

05:24.380 --> 05:26.330
I asked the teacher earlier,

05:26.330 --> 05:30.140
and Miki-chan entered the orphanage six months ago.

05:30.410 --> 05:31.890
Is that so?

05:31.890 --> 05:37.900
Miki-chan's parents tried to include her in a family suicide.

05:38.240 --> 05:40.650
After almost being killed by her own parents,

05:40.650 --> 05:43.670
she doesn't trust other people anymore.

05:43.670 --> 05:47.440
Ever since then, she's avoided contact with everyone.

05:47.440 --> 05:49.470
She won't socialize with others,

05:49.470 --> 05:52.770
and apparently she won't eat unless she's alone.

05:52.770 --> 05:56.910
No one has tried to adopt her,
and she's been shutting herself away.

05:56.910 --> 05:58.670
I see.

05:58.670 --> 06:02.670
I wonder if there really is no God anywhere.

06:04.670 --> 06:09.260
Because there is no God, many sad and painful things occur.

06:09.260 --> 06:13.920
If there really was a God, then I'd want him to make this world more beautiful.

06:13.920 --> 06:20.310
A world where there's no hardship, where everyone is kind, and no one is left alone.

06:20.310 --> 06:21.810
Yeah.

06:22.260 --> 06:23.520
Yu-kun?

06:23.520 --> 06:25.030
If only...

06:25.420 --> 06:30.030
If only such a convenient world could be created...

06:30.030 --> 06:32.030
the

06:32.210 --> 06:35.790
If only there was something I could do to transform this world like that.

06:38.040 --> 06:40.420
Did something happen, Yu?

06:40.420 --> 06:42.580
Not really. Why?

06:42.580 --> 06:44.480
Your lines are different from usual.

06:44.480 --> 06:46.080
"Different"?

06:46.080 --> 06:48.710
Did they get better? Or did they get worse?

06:48.710 --> 06:50.440
There's no bewilderment in your lines.

06:50.440 --> 06:51.970
You've improved.

06:51.970 --> 06:52.720
Really?

06:52.720 --> 06:53.660
Yeah.

06:53.660 --> 06:56.700
Although you're still below a passing grade.

06:59.110 --> 07:00.600
Oh yeah, Nagi.

07:00.600 --> 07:01.710
What?

07:01.710 --> 07:05.150
Will I get better at nude sketches as I draw more of them?

07:05.150 --> 07:09.030
Not really, but it's something you should do at least once.

07:09.030 --> 07:10.720
I see...

07:10.720 --> 07:12.700
Nagi, would you undress?

07:15.810 --> 07:16.700
No.

07:16.700 --> 07:17.910
Why not?!

07:17.910 --> 07:20.790
It's a bit embarrassing to actually be asked to take off my clothes.

07:20.790 --> 07:22.670
What's with that?

07:22.670 --> 07:25.170
But I'll let you use this, instead.

07:25.410 --> 07:27.200
Why a mirror?

07:27.200 --> 07:31.340
As long as it's a real person, it doesn't have to be a woman.

07:31.340 --> 07:32.120
Perfect.

07:32.120 --> 07:33.970
I was actually thinking about how I wanted to draw you, too.

07:34.510 --> 07:37.600
You go ahead and undress. No one's going to care.

07:37.600 --> 07:39.810
I'll care!

07:56.380 --> 07:57.580
Miki-chan.

07:59.580 --> 08:00.770
Wait!

08:04.130 --> 08:06.380
Miki-chan, I have something to ask you.

08:06.980 --> 08:10.020
Could you help me?

08:10.020 --> 08:11.260
Please.

08:20.160 --> 08:21.230
What is it?

08:21.230 --> 08:24.330
I'm very lonely right now.

08:24.330 --> 08:28.650
I have someone who's precious to me,
but he's at work right now.

08:28.650 --> 08:31.510
I can't see him until nighttime, when he comes home,

08:31.510 --> 08:33.650
and because of that, I'm really lonely.

08:33.900 --> 08:35.910
Weakling.

08:35.910 --> 08:39.160
If he's going to come back,
then you shouldn't be lonely at all.

08:41.160 --> 08:42.220
I see.

08:42.220 --> 08:43.960
Miki-chan, you're strong, aren't you?

08:44.660 --> 08:47.340
I'm weak, so I'm lonely.

08:47.340 --> 08:50.090
Could you stay with me for a little while?

08:51.790 --> 08:54.090
Thank you, Miki-chan.

08:56.970 --> 08:59.140
Miki-chan, do you have any friends?

08:59.140 --> 09:00.160
No.

09:00.160 --> 09:01.270
Why not?

09:01.270 --> 09:02.630
Because I don't need them!

09:02.630 --> 09:04.230
It's fun to have them, you know.

09:04.610 --> 09:05.850
But I still don't need them.

09:06.310 --> 09:07.600
I see.

09:07.850 --> 09:09.610
How lonely.

09:09.610 --> 09:10.940
Why?

09:10.940 --> 09:14.360
Because I thought you could be my friend.

09:16.040 --> 09:17.360
Is that impossible?

09:18.790 --> 09:20.490
No, it's fine.

09:20.800 --> 09:21.830
Really?

09:22.520 --> 09:23.700
Yeah.

09:23.700 --> 09:26.710
Well, in that case, will you shake my hand?

09:26.710 --> 09:27.580
Okay?

09:35.280 --> 09:36.840
Please, help me!

09:39.730 --> 09:41.220
Thank you.

09:41.220 --> 09:43.680
Then, you're not lonely anymore?

09:43.680 --> 09:46.930
Yeah! I'm not lonely anymore.

09:52.690 --> 09:54.190
Yuko.

09:54.860 --> 09:57.570
I thought you'd be here.

10:01.870 --> 10:04.370
She fell asleep while we were talking.

10:04.690 --> 10:06.260
She's going to catch a cold.

10:06.260 --> 10:08.250
I'd feel bad if I woke her up.

10:12.750 --> 10:17.130
This way, it's like you covered Miki-chan up.

10:17.130 --> 10:18.770
I'm not that good of a person, you know.

10:18.770 --> 10:20.380
You're really stubborn, aren't you?

10:22.840 --> 10:24.390
Miki-chan?

10:26.190 --> 10:27.140
I'm scared...

10:28.270 --> 10:30.980
My dream... was scary.

10:31.870 --> 10:34.980
It's all right. I'm here.

10:37.880 --> 10:39.490
Good night.

10:48.500 --> 10:51.250
Strength

10:51.250 --> 10:53.750
Yu-kun, are you still awake?

10:53.750 --> 10:54.650
Yeah.

10:54.650 --> 10:56.800
Can I come over to your side?

10:56.800 --> 10:57.510
Yeah.

11:02.260 --> 11:04.430
Why are you facing the other way?

11:04.430 --> 11:07.100
It'll be warmer if our backs are touching.

11:09.320 --> 11:12.040
You're right. It's warm.

11:12.040 --> 11:15.870
When I was little, I'd do this with Akane during the winter.

11:15.870 --> 11:18.110
My house was pretty cold, too.

11:18.380 --> 11:19.940
Is that so?

11:19.940 --> 11:21.630
Yu-kun, did you know?

11:21.630 --> 11:25.870
In Australia, Christmas comes in the summer, so I've heard it's hot then.

11:25.870 --> 11:27.750
Because Australia's in the southern hemisphere.

11:27.750 --> 11:29.620
Conversely, it's winter in July.

11:29.620 --> 11:31.570
A Christmas in the summer...

11:31.570 --> 11:35.380
I wonder what it's like? I'd like to see it.

11:35.380 --> 11:38.250
Simply setting up a Christmas tree during Tanabata would do.

11:35.380 --> 11:38.250
Tanabata: A Japanese star festival that celebrates the meeting of Orihime (Vega) and Hikoboshi (Altair).

11:38.830 --> 11:43.010
I wonder if a miracle would happen and Christmas would occur in the summer?

11:43.340 --> 11:45.340
Miracles don't exist in this world.

11:45.340 --> 11:49.520
The only things that exist are coincidences and inevitabilities, and the actions people take.

11:49.520 --> 11:51.390
You're really not a dreamer, are you?

11:51.390 --> 11:53.890
If you want to dream, hurry up and go to sleep already.

11:53.890 --> 11:55.400
Geez...

11:55.830 --> 11:57.210
Night.

11:57.210 --> 11:58.680
Good night.

12:10.100 --> 12:12.710
Hello, Miki-chan.

12:12.710 --> 12:14.210
Yuko!

12:14.210 --> 12:16.960
the

12:16.960 --> 12:18.880
I see. A dream?

12:18.880 --> 12:20.290
I always have it.

12:20.290 --> 12:22.600
Although I didn't have it the day I met you.

12:22.600 --> 12:23.630
Is that so?

12:23.950 --> 12:25.130
Yeah.

12:25.130 --> 12:28.890
I see. Maybe that's because we held hands?

12:29.140 --> 12:30.640
Hands?

12:30.640 --> 12:32.310
Would you like to try?

12:35.020 --> 12:36.350
How is it?

12:36.650 --> 12:38.310
Warm.

12:38.310 --> 12:40.370
You'll be fine now.

12:40.370 --> 12:41.360
What about tomorrow?

12:41.360 --> 12:42.400
Huh?

12:42.400 --> 12:44.070
Will you hold hands with me tomorrow, too?

12:44.400 --> 12:45.820
Sure!

12:49.800 --> 12:55.080
With the courage to live

12:55.080 --> 13:00.350
and a future to embrace...

13:00.350 --> 13:01.660
What is that?

13:01.660 --> 13:04.840
It's a song that a friend of mine played for me a long time ago.

13:05.460 --> 13:09.720
I was in a lot of pain, and I hated this world,

13:10.060 --> 13:13.220
and this song was so beautiful that when I heard it,

13:13.220 --> 13:18.770
it made me think, "Perhaps there are things in this world that I could come to love".

13:18.770 --> 13:20.550
And my heart wavered.

13:20.550 --> 13:24.120
It was painful at the time, but now I've been saved.

13:24.120 --> 13:27.450
I can listen to this song with open feelings now.

13:27.620 --> 13:28.830
Yuko...

13:28.830 --> 13:31.160
I made up these lyrics, you know.

13:31.160 --> 13:32.890
Although the song's incomplete.

13:33.800 --> 13:35.310
Could you sing it one more time?

13:35.310 --> 13:37.600
It's not complete yet!

13:37.600 --> 13:38.700
That's fine.

13:38.700 --> 13:39.740
Really?

13:40.100 --> 13:45.480
ikiru yuuki to

13:40.100 --> 13:45.480
With the courage to live

13:45.480 --> 13:50.450
ikiru yuuki to

13:45.480 --> 13:50.450
With the courage to live

13:50.450 --> 13:55.830
idaku mirai to

13:50.450 --> 13:55.830
and a future to embrace...

13:55.830 --> 14:01.000
idaku mirai to

13:55.830 --> 14:01.000
and a future to embrace...

14:01.000 --> 14:06.700
minna ga kureta tsuyosa

14:01.000 --> 14:06.700
and the strength that everyone gave you

14:06.700 --> 14:12.440
minna ga kureta tsuyosa

14:06.700 --> 14:12.440
and the strength that everyone gave you

14:12.440 --> 14:17.820
ai wo shinjite

14:12.440 --> 14:17.820
put your trust in love.

14:17.820 --> 14:23.000
ai wo shinjite

14:17.820 --> 14:23.000
put your trust in love.

14:23.000 --> 14:26.510
When white snow falls

14:23.000 --> 14:26.510
It enwraps and hides the color of sorrow

14:30.680 --> 14:32.340
You're with that girl again?

14:32.340 --> 14:34.970
I'm not "that girl". I'm Miki.

14:37.910 --> 14:41.350
Well then, please hold out your hand too, Yu-kun.

14:41.940 --> 14:43.360
Here!

14:47.530 --> 14:48.800
Isn't this great?

14:48.800 --> 14:51.510
With this much hand-holding, you should be fine.

14:51.510 --> 14:52.110
Yeah!

14:52.450 --> 14:54.120
You won't cry anymore?

14:55.420 --> 14:57.680
I don't know.

14:57.680 --> 15:00.620
Girls should always smile, you know.

15:00.790 --> 15:02.000
How come?

15:02.000 --> 15:07.170
If you make a sad face just because you're sad,
then sad things will truly happen.

15:07.170 --> 15:09.350
But if you smile,

15:09.350 --> 15:12.930
someday the smile will become real, and the sadness will disappear.

15:12.930 --> 15:14.180
Really?

15:14.180 --> 15:14.980
Yeah.

15:14.980 --> 15:17.330
So let's smile all the time.

15:17.330 --> 15:19.810
Okay! I won't cry anymore.

15:22.670 --> 15:25.480
I want to make a beautiful city.

15:26.400 --> 15:30.240
I don't want to just decorate and patch the surface of a ruin,

15:30.240 --> 15:32.660
but make a truly beautiful city.

15:32.660 --> 15:36.990
A city where everyone is kind, and no one will be alone.

15:36.990 --> 15:39.160
A bright city that's connected to the future.

15:39.330 --> 15:41.250
Yu-kun...

15:41.710 --> 15:42.920
Yeah.

15:43.360 --> 15:45.750
I'm sure you can do it, Yu-kun.

15:48.080 --> 15:50.920
Thank goodness. Miki-chan is more cheerful now.

15:55.930 --> 15:57.810
It's from Kuze from Germany.

15:58.210 --> 16:00.180
What did Kuze-san say?

16:00.760 --> 16:02.980
He says, "German girls are the best".

16:02.980 --> 16:04.060
Oh my.

16:04.060 --> 16:07.190
Also, he's coming back to Japan for Christmas.

16:07.190 --> 16:08.860
For Christmas?

16:08.860 --> 16:13.990
But he said that he might not have time to see us, because he's already promised to meet a girl.

16:15.360 --> 16:18.990
Yu-kun, what are you doing for Christmas?

16:18.990 --> 16:20.740
If it's all right, let's—

16:20.740 --> 16:23.160
I have to work on Christmas morning.

16:23.160 --> 16:25.620
I'm leaving home earlier than usual, to help stock the store.

16:25.620 --> 16:27.630
Is that so?

16:29.000 --> 16:32.920
But in exchange, I've asked to be let off earlier in the afternoon.

16:34.090 --> 16:35.970
Shall we go somewhere?

16:36.320 --> 16:37.270
Yes!

16:37.270 --> 16:39.220
Let's meet at our usual church.

16:39.220 --> 16:41.150
I'll be there as soon as my work is done.

16:41.150 --> 16:43.740
Okay, I'll go on ahead and wait for you.

16:43.740 --> 16:45.730
Please don't be late, okay?

16:50.480 --> 16:51.730
I see.

16:51.730 --> 16:54.860
You're spending Christmas alone with Yuko-chan tonight?

16:54.860 --> 16:56.280
Nagi.

16:57.030 --> 16:59.030
But a bouquet of flowers?

16:59.030 --> 17:02.120
It's an item that absolutely doesn't fit Himura Yu.

17:02.120 --> 17:03.730
None of your business.

17:03.730 --> 17:06.120
But it fits Yuko-chan.

17:06.120 --> 17:07.310
Ah, really?

17:07.310 --> 17:10.170
Yeah. Yuko-chan and flowers go well together.

17:18.180 --> 17:20.930
we

17:54.340 --> 17:56.590
What is it, young lady?

17:56.590 --> 17:58.470
That song just now...

17:58.470 --> 18:00.210
Did you like it?

18:00.210 --> 18:01.350
Yeah.

18:01.350 --> 18:02.720
I see.

18:11.730 --> 18:12.950
Here.

18:12.950 --> 18:14.730
You look cuter this way.

18:14.730 --> 18:16.230
Really?!

18:16.230 --> 18:17.490
Yup.

18:22.870 --> 18:25.370
Thank you!

18:28.120 --> 18:30.870
Times

18:42.930 --> 18:45.430
Maybe I came a little too early.

18:53.340 --> 18:54.860
Geez...

19:06.330 --> 19:09.220
Just how long are you going to follow me around?

19:09.220 --> 19:13.010
I'm interested in what you're going to say to her when you give her that bouquet.

19:13.010 --> 19:14.250
Seriously...

19:14.250 --> 19:15.650
I'm joking.

19:15.650 --> 19:18.000
I don't intend to interrupt your date.

19:18.130 --> 19:19.780
Geez.

19:19.780 --> 19:20.590
Huh?

19:20.760 --> 19:22.340
Well, if it isn't Miki.

19:22.340 --> 19:23.340
What's up?

19:25.120 --> 19:26.100
That!

19:26.600 --> 19:28.430
It's an Angel's Staircase.

19:28.430 --> 19:29.600
Angel's Staircase?

19:29.600 --> 19:34.810
Yeah. They say angels go up and down in that light.

19:39.610 --> 19:44.110
There are still... many things I want to talk to you about.

19:44.620 --> 19:50.620
I want... you... to know more about me.

19:52.420 --> 19:58.330
The courage to live...

19:59.620 --> 20:06.850
and a future... to embrace...

20:06.850 --> 20:14.410
and... the strength... that everyone... gave me...

20:15.770 --> 20:20.670
Putting...

20:20.670 --> 20:27.160
our... trust...

20:30.950 --> 20:34.500
I want to meet Yu-kun once more.

20:42.750 --> 20:45.770
Love, I've got to feel it

20:46.050 --> 20:49.100
If you put your trust in me

20:49.370 --> 20:52.620
I know what my life would be

20:52.690 --> 20:57.510
Oh, you are all I ever need

20:57.670 --> 21:03.210
I try to hear what you say

21:03.360 --> 21:05.480
So I pray

21:05.560 --> 21:09.060
But you're fading away

21:10.500 --> 21:16.220
Don't go and break my fragile heart

21:16.650 --> 21:19.850
We won't fall apart

21:19.970 --> 21:28.030
'Cause you're my only star

21:29.990 --> 21:33.740
I wonder why my tears come at night

21:33.740 --> 21:37.250
Calling you, so like a little child

21:37.410 --> 21:40.490
All the things you have in mind

21:40.750 --> 21:43.870
I wish I could see your insides

21:43.870 --> 21:46.900
My love, you've got to feel it

21:46.900 --> 21:50.210
And if we put our trust in you and me

21:50.420 --> 21:53.870
You know what our lives would be

21:53.990 --> 22:01.830
Oh, you are the one, I believe

22:35.450 --> 22:41.330
Somehow, it feels that our reunion happened in the distant past.

22:41.330 --> 22:42.790
You're right.

22:45.510 --> 22:49.060
It'll probably become even more distant soon, won't it?

22:49.060 --> 22:50.550
No way.

22:52.090 --> 22:54.930
I'm going to entrust this to you, Yu-kun.

22:55.530 --> 22:56.600
To me?

22:56.600 --> 23:00.560
This was a place where I could be alone.

23:00.560 --> 23:04.120
A place where I could cry, knowing that no one would see.

23:04.120 --> 23:08.360
But I'm not alone anymore, and I won't cry anymore either.

23:08.680 --> 23:10.110
Yuko...

23:10.110 --> 23:12.850
That's why I want to give it away.

23:12.850 --> 23:14.780
So that I won't look back on my past anymore.

23:14.780 --> 23:17.490
Please give it to someone who needs it.

23:17.830 --> 23:19.110
I got it.

23:19.110 --> 23:20.450
I'll hold on to it.

23:26.320 --> 23:30.540
Please, let my wishes reach him.

23:30.540 --> 23:33.620
ef - a tale of melodies.

23:33.620 --> 23:35.730
Reread.

23:35.730 --> 23:39.790
Can you hear it? The melody of truth.
